//? Title: Grad-CAM and Grad-CAM++:coarse maps with explicit score assumptions
//? Requires: vanilla_saliency.mepml
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Image-level digit scores do not reveal which coarse convolutional features influence them. Freeze the verified MNIST classifier and compute both Grad-CAM and an explicit locally-affine exp-score Grad-CAM++formulation,with original images,all intermediates and target/weight controls.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.11_interpretability/grad_cam.cpp`.

> The method

For last post-ReLU featuresAand fixed raw scoreS,letg=dS/dA. Classic channel weights are spatial means ofg. Grad-CAM++uses positive-gradient pixel weights derived from exp(S-c),withc held fixed at the currentS and locally affine downstreamS:

$$ w_k=\operatorname{mean}_{ij}g_{ijk},\quad CAM=ReLU(\sum_k w_k A_k),\quad\alpha_{ijk}=\frac{1[g_{ijk}>0]}{2+g_{ijk}\sum_{ab}A_{abk}}. $$
\alttext(Classic channel weights average raw-score gradients;the classic map rectifies their weighted features. Positive Grad-CAM++alpha uses the explicitly derived exp-score expression and is zero for nonpositive gradients.)

The implementation masks irrelevant nonpositive-gradient denominators safely. It does not label first-gradient powers as rawlogit higher derivatives. Every numerical model,derivative,formula,normalization,metric and plotting value uses tensors;the classifier fitting loop is in vanilla_saliency.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/grad_cam_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/grad_cam_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/grad_cam_concept.tikz > build/grad_cam_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/grad_cam_concept.svg build/grad_cam_concept.dvi > build/grad_cam_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
