> Hand-checkable channel weights and exp-score derivatives

The declared two-batch,two-channel fixture exposes every channel weight,
positive alpha and raw map. Native tests independently verify every formula,
zero-map normalization,and24actual first/second/third derivatives of exp(affineS).
For Grad-CAM++,useY=exp(S-c),wherec is fixed at the currentS. Inside a fixed
hidden-ReLU region,Sis affine inAandY=1at the evaluation point. Its diagonal
first/second/third derivatives areg,g squared,g cubed. The RAWlogit's second
and third derivatives are locallyzero;they are not those powers.

For positiveg,paperEq19cancelsg squared toalpha=1/(2+sum_spatial(A)*g).
For g<=0,the ReLUgradient contribution vanishes and alpha is explicitly0.
Post-ReLUnonnegativeAkeeps relevant denominators at least2. This formulation
requires a locally affine downstream score and does not claim general smooth
nonlinear heads satisfy the same derivative identities.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/grad_cam_fixture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto activation = n::arange(1, 17).reshape({2, 2, 2, 2}) * .05;
  const auto g = n::from_vector(std::vector<float>{.3f, -.2f, 0, .4f, -.1f, .2f, .5f, 0, .3f,
                                                   -.2f, 0, .4f, -.1f, .2f, .5f, 0},
                                {2, 2, 2, 2});
  const auto maps = m::ClassActivationMaps(activation, g);
  std::print("Declared spatial mean weights {},positivealpha {},plusweights {}.\n",
             maps.grad_weights, maps.positive_alpha, maps.plus_weights);
  std::print("Raw signed classic {},rectifiedclassic {},plus {};allzero normalized {}.\n",
             maps.grad_signed, maps.grad_map, maps.plus_map,
             m::NormalizeCam(n::zeros({1, 2, 2})));
  const auto peak = n::max(n::stack({n::max(maps.grad_map), n::max(maps.plus_map)}, 0)).item();
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(n::select(maps.grad_map, 0, 0), {0}), 0, peak),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(n::select(maps.plus_map, 0, 0), {0}), 0, peak);
  a.title("Declared raw Grad-CAM").x_label("feature x").y_label("feature y");
  b.title("Declared raw Grad-CAM++").x_label("feature x").y_label("feature y");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg("build/grad_cam_fixture.svg");
}
