The chosen true digit4is misclassified as9;its selected-target map therefore
explains the model's9score,and the runner-up map uses4. No map changes that
classification error.

> Complete per-case target and weight controls

Compare normalized coarse maps by cosine,including zero-safe cases;retain raw
map magnitudes and the actual selected-vs-runner category IDs. These controls
test dependence,not explanation quality. A normalized allzero classic map stays
zero rather than becomingNaN. Actual mean plus-map cosines are.998598319for the runner,.971336165for full
initialization,and.999975561for head reset. These near-identical normalized
responses limit evidence of target/head dependence. Classic-map corresponding
means are.688794081/.539342060/.960113744. No superiority claim follows from
either attractive gallery.

The two methods can produce different maps even
though they use the same raw-score first derivatives and frozen classifier.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/grad_cam_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto &[key, value] : n::load_npz("build/grad_cam_maps.npz"))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  std::vector<n::Tensor> classic, plus;
  std::print("| control | mean classic cosine | mean plus cosine |\n|---|---:|---:|\n");
  for (const std::string control : {"runner", "initial", "head_initial"}) {
    std::vector<n::Tensor> pair;
    for (const std::string method : {"cam_normalized", "plus_normalized"}) {
      const auto x = a.at("trained_" + method).to(n::DType::Float64).reshape({10, 196}),
                 y = a.at(control + "_" + method).to(n::DType::Float64).reshape({10, 196});
      const auto scale = n::sqrt(n::sum(n::square(x), {1}) * n::sum(n::square(y), {1}));
      const auto cosine =
          n::sum(x * y, {1}) / n::maximum(scale, n::full({10}, 1e-30, n::DType::Float64));
      pair.push_back(cosine);
    }
    classic.push_back(pair[0]);
    plus.push_back(pair[1]);
    std::print("| {} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} |\n", control, n::mean(pair[0]).item(),
               n::mean(pair[1]).item());
  }
  const auto difference =
      n::sum(n::abs(a.at("trained_cam_normalized") - a.at("trained_plus_normalized")));
  const auto zero =
      n::sum(n::equal(n::max(a.at("trained_cam"), {1, 2}), 0.).to(n::DType::Int32));
  std::print("All1960normalized selectedmethod pixels L1difference {:.9g};allzero classic "
             "cases {};fixed targets {},runners {}.\n",
             difference.item(), zero.item(), a.at("targets"), a.at("runners"));
  auto left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  const std::vector<std::string> labels{"runner", "initial", "head reset"};
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}, {22, 163, 74}};
  for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
    left.lines(n::arange(0, 10).to_vector<double>(), classic[i].to_vector<double>(), labels[i],
               colors[i]);
    right.lines(n::arange(0, 10).to_vector<double>(), plus[i].to_vector<double>(), labels[i],
                colors[i]);
  }
  left.title("Every classic-map control")
      .x_label("true digit0..9")
      .y_label("normalized-map cosine")
      .y_limits(-.05, 1.15);
  right.title("Every plus-map control")
      .x_label("true digit0..9")
      .y_label("normalized-map cosine")
      .y_limits(-.05, 1.15);
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(left).add(right).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/grad_cam_controls.svg");
}
```
